Story: First cup
  As a tea drinker
  I want to start the kettle by turning the dial
  So that it works like the one I already have

  The kettle starts the way an old stovetop knob does: drag the DIAL slider past 55 % and the
  kettle starts a moment later. The light turns red and the [[display]] reads HEATING.

  The dial is only a switch. How hot the water gets is the preset on the display, WARM (70 °C)
  unless you change it (see [[Choosing a preset]]). The WATER line shows the temperature as it
  rises, and the kettle holds the water there until you turn it off. To turn it off, bring the
  dial back down first, then press RESET; with the dial still up, RESET would only start it
  again.

  Scenario: Turn it up, then turn it off
    When the dial is 80 %
    Then the kettle is heating
    When the dial is 0 %
    And the user presses reset
    Then the kettle is off

Story: Keeping little hands off
  As a parent
  I want the child lock to keep the kettle off
  So that a curious toddler turning the dial doesn't start it

  LOCK turns the child lock on and off, and the LOCK badge lights up while it is on. While it is
  on, the dial, START and PRESET do nothing, so a turned dial cannot start the kettle.

  The lock stops the dial from reaching the kettle; it does not move the dial. If the dial is
  still above 55 % when you unlock, the kettle starts as soon as the lock comes off. So bring
  the dial down before you press LOCK again, as this tutorial does.

  Scenario: Turn the dial with the lock on, then unlock and boil
    When the user presses lock
    Then the child lock is on
    When the dial is 100 %
    Then the kettle is off
    When the dial is 0 %
    And the user presses lock
    Then the child lock is off
    When the dial is 80 %
    Then the kettle is heating

Story: Choosing a preset
  As someone who drinks oolong
  I want to pick how hot the water gets before I start
  So that the water suits the leaves

  The preset is the temperature the kettle heats to and then holds: WARM is 70 °C, HOT is
  85 °C and BOIL is 100 °C. Green tea is usually made around 70 °C, oolong around 85 °C and
  black tea with boiling water. The kettle is on WARM when you open the app.

  PRESET steps through WARM, HOT and BOIL and back to WARM, and the PRESET line on the
  [[display]] shows the one you have. START starts the kettle without touching the dial.
  PRESET, like the other buttons, does nothing while the child lock is on.

  Scenario: Step to HOT and start
    When the user presses preset
    Then the preset is HOT
    When the user presses start
    Then the kettle is heating
